    <string name="privacy_identity">TimeWall privacy notice\nController: %1$s\nContact: %2$s</string>
    <string name="privacy_updated">Last updated: %1$s</string>
    <string name="privacy_service">Purpose and legal basis\nProcessing is necessary to provide the requested calendar dashboard and optional weather features (GDPR Article 6(1)(b)); legal obligations apply where relevant. TimeWall has no user accounts or developer backend and uses no advertising, analytics or profiling. It makes no automated decisions with legal effects.</string>
    <string name="privacy_calendars">Calendars\nThe app connects directly to the HTTPS iCal providers you configure. URLs, calendar names, colors and complete iCal files are stored locally; files may include titles, times, descriptions, locations, identifiers, creation dates and other personal data. Secret URLs grant calendar access: protect them and use only calendars you are authorized to access. Providers see the requested URL, connection IP and network metadata; their own privacy policies apply.</string>
    <string name="privacy_weather">Optional weather\nLocation searches and language are sent to Open-Meteo geocoding; forecasts send the coordinates of the place you choose. No GPS location is requested. Open-Meteo also sees the connection IP and states that API logs, potentially including coordinates, are deleted after 90 days. Disabling weather stops forecast updates; explicit searches in Settings still contact Open-Meteo. External providers act independently and may process data outside your country or the EEA; see their policies for locations and safeguards. The weather widget can refresh in the background when weather is enabled. The latest successful result is cached locally and shared with the dashboard.</string>
    <string name="privacy_local">Local settings and images\nTheme, font, language, filters, time format and weather preferences stay on the device. The background image is read through the Android file picker; TimeWall does not upload it. The controller receives personal data only if you choose to contact them, such as your email address and message, to handle that request.</string>
    <string name="privacy_retention">Retention and deletion\nCalendar caches are replaced on successful updates and removed when you save calendar removal or a URL change. Settings → Calendars → Clear calendar cache deletes local calendar copies and downloads them again; it does not remove configuration. Disabling weather keeps the selected place and settings. Clearing app data or uninstalling removes private app storage, not original images or provider-held data. Contact messages are retained for as long as needed to handle the request and applicable legal obligations.</string>
    <string name="privacy_security">Security\nNetwork requests use HTTPS. Local files and preferences rely on Android app isolation without additional application-level encryption. Weather error logs contain only fixed diagnostic categories. Android backup is disabled. Opening an external link uses your chosen browser or email app and is subject to that service’s policy.</string>
    <string name="privacy_rights">Your rights\nWhere applicable, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability and object to processing by contacting the controller. You may complain to the Italian Garante or another competent data protection authority. For device-only data, use local controls: the controller cannot access it remotely. For data held by independent calendar or weather providers, contact those providers. Providing a calendar URL or weather place is optional; without them the corresponding feature is unavailable.</string>
    <string name="privacy_web_pending">Public privacy-policy URL: to be defined.</string>
